// The cell on a controller: one instance of FB_{{cellName}}, and the cyclic OB that calls it.
//
// The station and coordinator patterns produce code that *compiles*. This is what makes it *run*,
// and it is a separate pattern because it is the only one that changes a block somebody else owns:
// a project already has a Main, and generating this replaces it. A caller that only wants the cell
// in the project should not be made to overwrite its entry point to get it.
//
// The OB calls the instance with **no parameters**, and that is the whole point of the file. Passing
// constants would assign the inputs on every scan, and then nothing outside the program could drive
// the cell: a tag write would land in the instance data block and be gone before the next call. With
// no parameters the inputs keep whatever was last written to them, which is what makes CellStart
// something a test, a watch table or an operator can actually set.
//
// The instance data block is named here rather than in the coordinator because its name is what
// every tag read has to spell: "DB_{{cellName}}".CellStart, "DB_{{cellName}}".{{firstStationName}}.Step.

DATA_BLOCK "DB_{{cellName}}"
{ S7_Optimized_Access := 'TRUE' }
"FB_{{cellName}}"
BEGIN
END_DATA_BLOCK

ORGANIZATION_BLOCK "Main"
{ S7_Optimized_Access := 'TRUE' }
VERSION : 0.1
BEGIN
    // Every scan, unconditionally. A cell that only runs when something enables it would need that
    // something to exist first, and there is nothing above the coordinator in this program.
    "DB_{{cellName}}"();
END_ORGANIZATION_BLOCK
